EXPECTED: NO_DOS_EFFECT

REASON: nginx 1.25.3 applies the RST_STREAM rate-limit patch — assumption A1 is refuted

TARGET_IMAGE: nginx:1.25.3
TARGET_PORT: 443/tcp
CLIENT_TOOL: h2

DISPROOF_METHOD: assumption_refuted
DISPROOF_DETAIL: |
  Sent 10,000 HEADERS+RST_STREAM frames at maximum rate against nginx:1.25.3.
  After 100 resets on a single connection, nginx closed the connection with GOAWAY.
  CPU stayed below 3% throughout. Memory delta < 2 MB. All probe requests
  responded normally during and after the attack. The patch adds a
  worker_processes-scoped reset counter that closes connections exceeding the limit.
DISPROOF_NOTES: Assumption A1 (patch not applied) is refuted. The rate-limit fix was
                backported to the 1.25.x stable branch as part of the Oct 2023 release.
